 "notes": [
  "No zonal office address and no hospital/UPHC table in this zone's appendix. Chairman row has no phone number printed (phones: []).",
  "Two numbers are printed as ranges and could not be recorded as phones: Conservancy Inspectors 'Div 109-126' = '9445190609 to 626', and CMWSSB Area Engineer '109 to 126' = '8144930109 to 126' (likely one number per ward, but the individual numbers are not printed). Range text kept in the designation; phones left empty.",
  "Conservancy supervisors appear with different numbers in two tables: SWM table (p.520) 9445190618/9445190625/9445190616/9445190615 for Units 24-27, and TNSCB contact-details table (p.525) 9445191424-9445191427. Both sets kept.",
  "The Park Overseer row (p.521) has no phone number, so it is not in officials. Senior Entomologist printed '98413 20440' (space removed); the same number is the Junior Entomologist in Zone 8.",
  "Names copied as printed, including 'Mr,Sathish' (comma). 'Mr.Venkatesh Siva-nathan' and 'Mr.Venkata Sivara-makumar' were hyphenated across lines and are joined.",
  "inundation_streets = the 16-row heavy-rain table (pp.529-530). Disposal 'Mamabalam Canal' is printed so (Mambalam). Some rows name 2-3 streets that share one pump; these were kept as single rows.",
  "Sewer-block table (pp.536-537, 17 rows, 57 manholes) lists several streets per row; split into one water_stagnation entry per street (17 rows became 38 entries). Moderate-rain rows such as 'Dr.Besant Road, Jnc. Of T.P. Koil Street' were not split, because they describe a single spot.",
  "Relief centres: 5 rows, total 4450, which matches the intro. Row 2 name is printed 'Chennai High chool, East machivayapuram' (probably Chennai High School, East Namachivayapuram) and is copied as printed. Row 1 streets 'Namachiya / puram' were wrapped across lines and joined as 'Namachiyapuram'. Row 4 (ward 111) is one table cell listing about 7 buildings (ICDS Centre, Chennai High School and Middle School at Model School Road, Community Hall, Jain Kalyana Mandapam, CSI Primary School, local Library Building); the map legend on p.540 gives them as R4-R10. ARO has two numbers (9445190709, 9445190089) for rows 1-4; row 5 lists only 9445190089. Row 2's Relief-Materials AE is 9445190418 (the AE of row 1), and its Evacuation AE is 9445190409.",
  "Water-entered-houses table: intro says 28 spots (4,310 people, 32 pumps of 5-30 HP); the table has 9 ward rows of comma-separated streets, split into one entry per street (31 entries).",
  "Tree fall: 17 ward rows split into one entry per street. Ward 123 'C.P.Ram,aswamy Road' is printed with a stray comma (C.P.Ramaswamy Road) and is kept as one entry. Intro: 66 trees/branches fell.",
  "Parks: 16 ward rows split into individual parks (36, which matches the intro count). For ward 122 'Turnbulls Road' and ward 113 'Kodambakkam High Road' only the road is given. Row 16 'Marina Beach Park' spans wards '114,116, 120,121 &125'.",
  "Evacuation table year is '2015' (zone 8 used '2015-16'). Relief-centre cell 'Community Centre at K.B.Dasn Rosd' is printed so.",
  "Sewage pumping stations: no ward given; the pump-motor column is not in the schema. Ward/name pairs in the population table differ slightly in spelling from other tables (Kosimani/Ammer/Ameer, Azat/Azt).",
  "NDRF Commandant phone printed '04177 – 246594/246269'; second number recorded as 04177-246269 assuming the shared STD code. Rescue-boat AEs were also added to officials.",
